# Grothendieck tribute — Part 56: arrow form of the Zariski topology

Alexandre Grothendieck (1928-2014).

Extension Phase 5 (#2159, EPIC #1646).

Parts 1-55 established the fundamentals: categories, sieves, topologies,
lattice laws, pullback identities, bases of sheaves, covering closure,
calibration, subcanonicity, dense topologies, sheaves, internal hom,
Cech cohomology, Mayer-Vietoris limits, Kan extensions, adjunctions,
monads, equivalences, monoidal categories, the Grothendieck construction,
the direct/exceptional image, the arrow form of coverage, the coherence
laws of the pullback pseudofunctor, the indexed lattice laws, the arrow
form of the dense, extreme topologies, of the pushforward-pullback
adjunction, of the bind, of the topology generated by a pretopology,
of the topology induced along a functor, of cover-preserving functors,
of the composition laws of these functors, of the topology generated
by a `Coverage`-style coverage, and of the topology generated by a
precoverage.

This part applies the "arrow form" thread to the **Zariski topology on
the category of schemes** — the first *named* concrete topology of the
series (after the dense topology of Part 44, defined on an abstract
category). Mathlib provides `Scheme.zariskiPretopology :=
pretopology @IsOpenImmersion`, the bridge `Scheme.zariskiTopology_eq`
(`zariskiTopology = zariskiPretopology.toGrothendieck`) and the
pointwise characterization `Pretopology.mem_toGrothendieck`, but **no
law connects the Zariski topology to the arrow form** `J.Covers`. We
fill the gap with six original theorems:

  - `covers_iff_zariski` (central, P54 template instantiated): for
    schemes `X Y`, an arrow `f : Y ⟶ X` and a sieve `S` on `X`,
    `Scheme.zariskiTopology.Covers S f ↔ ∃ R ∈ Scheme.zariskiPretopology Y,
    R ≤ (S.pullback f).arrows` — arrow coverage is tested on `Y` by the
    existence of a covering family of open immersions refining the
    pullback.
  - `covers_iff_exists_cover` (Zariski-specific, signature theorem):
    `Scheme.zariskiTopology.Covers S f ↔ ∃ 𝒰 : Y.Cover (precoverage
    IsOpenImmersion), Presieve.ofArrows 𝒰.X 𝒰.f ≤ S.pullback f` — in
    the world of schemes, covering means **being refined by a concrete
    open cover** (`Scheme.Cover`). This is the geometric
    characterization of the arrow form, absent from the generic level
    of Parts 52-54 (which operate on an abstract pretopology, with no
    concrete "cover" object).
  - `covers_zariski_of_mem` (base case): if `R` is a covering family
    for the Zariski pretopology, the sieve it generates covers the
    identity.
  - `covers_zariski_of_mem_arrow` (generalized case): the coverage
    generated by `R ∈ zariskiPretopology X` covers any arrow
    `f : Y ⟶ X` — the refinement descends to `Y` via `pullbackArrows`,
    the base-change stability of the pretopology.
  - `covers_zariski_top`: the trivial coverage `⊤` covers any arrow —
    the witness is `Presieve.singleton (𝟙 Y)`, admitted by the
    `has_isos` axiom of pretopologies (the identity is an open
    immersion).
  - `covers_iff_pullback_zariski` (pointwise fallout): covering along
    the identity is equivalent to belonging to the topology.

Each proof is a **real tactic proof** (MED vein): Mathlib axioms
(`GrothendieckTopology.covers_iff`, `Scheme.zariskiTopology_eq`,
`Pretopology.mem_toGrothendieck`, `Scheme.mem_grothendieckTopology_iff`,
`Sieve.pullback_id`, `Sieve.le_generate`, `Sieve.generate_le_iff`,
`Sieve.pullbackArrows_comm`, `Pretopology.pullbacks`, `Pretopology.has_isos`,
`GrothendieckTopology.covering_iff_covers_id`) composed into a concrete
instantiation. No proof is a re-export or an unfold.

